caption: Cost Refinement results
technology-rule: cost-refinement-results

R_C 0: cost falls 1 percentage point per MoS; minimum Cost Factor 25.

R_C 1: cost falls 5 percentage points per MoS; minimum Cost Factor 20.

R_C 2: cost falls 10 percentage points per MoS; minimum Cost Factor 15.

R_C 3: cost falls 15 percentage points per MoS; minimum Cost Factor 10.

R_C 4: cost falls 20 percentage points per MoS; minimum Cost Factor 5.

R_C 5: cost falls 25 percentage points per MoS; minimum Cost Factor 5.

Additional Cost Refinement beyond four does not lower the hard floor below 5. It allows the designer to reach that floor with a smaller invention margin.

The Prototype roll fixes the costs of that formula. Manufacturing the same formula later does not recalculate its Cost Factor.

A formula may be optimized later as a new invention.

Separate chems have separate costs. Mixing them costs the sum of the component doses.
